findings=[
 {'id':'Q324','title':'Leaf replacement keeps a retired Path-B scene and discards the replacement paint','source':'crates/cambium/sprigging/src/lib.rs:271,401,412','status':'verified original current Sprigging registry/cache API over three exact retained suppliers; no live product replacement or GPU execution','evidence':'LeafRegistry and RenderedLeaves independently retain state by the same numeric key, without a leaf incarnation. After a SceneSlot is painted, replacing it under the same key with a fresh Swatch repaints but cx.take_scene().or(prior_scene) selects the retired scene, discards the new rect commands, and continues publishing DrawExternalTexture. Removing and reinserting an empty SceneSlot of the same size instead skips paint entirely and retains retired content. Two actual registry/cache counterexamples pass. The carry is intended for a size-only repaint of the same scene leaf, but cannot distinguish a replacement. An in-tree live product replacement causing a physical wrong image was not established.','diagnostics':['sprigging_retention_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Qualify retained output by leaf incarnation/paint kind or explicitly invalidate both caches on replacement. Keep same-leaf SceneSlot size carry; changing .or alone would erase that valid behavior.'}},
 {'id':'Q325','title':'Public graph styling changes current hit geometry without dirtying retained paint','source':'crates/cambium/sprigging/src/glyphs.rs:181,315; crates/cambium/sprigging/src/lib.rs:282,401','status':'verified actual original GraphCanvas and cache APIs; live product style mutation/native hit dispatch not run','evidence':'GraphCanvas exposes node_radius and edge_width publicly but paint_dirty only reads its private flag; neither direct field assignment nor LeafRegistry::get_mut_as invalidates it. After the first render, adding 10 to node_radius moves node_local_position(0) by (10,10), yet render_into at unchanged size returns zero and retains byte-for-byte debug-equivalent old commands. Similar public colors and sizes exist on other stock leaves. This makes the advertised common paint/hit projection disagree across retention boundaries. The ordinary Cambium paint_leaf wrapper sets these fields on a newly constructed dirty leaf; that construction path is not shown failing.','diagnostics':['sprigging_retention_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Provide invalidating style setters or a revisioned paint-input snapshot. Avoid forcing every unchanged leaf to repaint merely because mutable access was requested.'}},
 {'id':'Q326','title':'Mesquite wheel selectors bypass the requested surface family','source':'crates/cambium/mesquite/src/probe.rs:36,176; crates/cambium/mesquite/src/wheel.rs:164','status':'source-verified current Mere adapter path plus inspected cached Taproot selector/driver implementation; full Mesquite runtime not compiled','evidence':'The wheel grammar retains surface:NAME via Selector::on_surface. Its app_step directly calls self.selector_target, then queues Wheel at Hit.point, without checking Hit.surface against the requested family. That selector_target applies the DOM/projection matcher and unconditionally attributes a match to P::SURFACE. The inspected cached Taproot matchers ignore surface because they match within a supplied DOM; its public resolve/click driving methods enforce matches_surface at the host boundary. The wheel verb bypasses those methods. Given a matching local control and a foreign surface name, the current branch still queues input for the local control. Ordinary shared click is protected by Taproot before click_target, so that path is not accused. No full current supplier build, scenario or OS wheel execution is claimed.','diagnostics':['capture_leaf_supplier_excerpt.txt'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Route wheel targeting through the scope-enforcing resolver or explicitly check selector.matches_surface(hit.surface). Keep the honest miss behavior and held-click semantics.'}},
 {'id':'Q327','title':'Standalone browser smoke keeps its PASS automation title after later errors','source':'crates/cambium/examples/genet_web_smoke/index.html:15,21; crates/cambium/examples/genet_web_smoke/src/lib.rs:399','status':'verified unchanged JavaScript error hooks in Node VM fixture storage; actual browser/GPU error timing not executed','evidence':'The HTML says console/window error hooks surface panics and JS failures through the title for external automation. Both hooks refuse to change any title beginning SMOKE, including SMOKE PASS. The Rust smoke sets that title after render submission and queue.present, without a separate completion/error boundary. The exact unchanged JS hooks correctly change a stage title to ERR for an early console error; after SMOKE PASS both console.error and the window error handler leave PASS. Errors still log to console, so this is a misleading title sentinel, not suppression of all diagnostics. The probe does not establish an observed browser/GPU fault.','diagnostics':['smoke_title_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Let observed failures revoke the automation sentinel and qualify success at the intended completion boundary. A submitted smoke frame does not prove eventual GPU completion or visible pixels.'}}
]
for f in findings:f['verification']=NAME
notes['findings'].extend(findings)
rows=[
 ('Mesquite centralizes both scenario receipt formats','The text compatibility module has no independent scenario pump.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lane.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/scenario.rs'], 'Both formats use Lane capture/close/acceptance lifecycle. Deliberate compatibility differences remain: text permits uniform nonblank frames and 120 presented-frame grace; JSON defaults to detail checks and eight. Do not misreport these documented differences as independent engines.'),
 ('Presentation admission differs from generic callback success','Native frames advance only for a new presentation; explicit windowless calls use a synthetic clock.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lane.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/capture.rs'], 'Unavailable redraws still poll capture completion; separate clock deadlines fail continuous presentation stalls and native GPU readback. Current tests explicitly use fake windows/delayed pixels. Complete source read is not freshly run native presentation proof.'),
 ('Paired capture owns immutable metadata at the presentation boundary','Native stamped pixels and sealed product projection have independent run/request/frame checks.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/pairing.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lane.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/capture.rs'], 'Checks refuse missing/foreign/stale identities, dimensions/scale disagreements and retained metadata budget excess. Product run freshness/redaction is caller-owned. Presentation serialization omits the newly carried context_generation while in-memory equality includes it; follow the intended durable identity contract before promoting a collision finding.'),
 ('Legacy capture snapshots are explicitly uncorrelated','Without capture_observer, fields are sampled later during readback collection.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lane.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lib.rs'], 'The code does not claim these legacy fields are a frozen presented-state projection. Paired mode is opt-in and backends must explicitly support it; the default refuses instead of inventing a stamp.'),
 ('Checkpoint state is shared rather than reimplemented by product verbs','Checkpoints gives read-only views of the Lane remember map.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/checkpoints.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/probe.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lib.rs'], 'same/differs/more/dropped use the same stored fields. Numeric dropped accepts f64 while more requires u64. Missing fields and failed comparisons return attributable errors. Original arithmetic tests were read, not rerun this pass.'),
 ('Wheel grammar is an admitted unshared copy of Taproot selectors','Mesquite restates the supplier-private selector parser.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/wheel.rs'], 'Source candidly explains the duplication and holds local tests, but separate tests do not enforce cross-package grammar equivalence. Q326 proves one host-scope rule was bypassed at the execution boundary, despite the parsed field surviving.'),
 ('Pixel-mask independence has a legitimate oracle purpose','Viewport transformation math intentionally does not call the engine transform under test.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/pixels.rs'], 'This is not competing product geometry authority: authored values are an independent check oracle. Comparisons reread saved PNGs, require equal retained viewport metadata and compare RGB with tolerance 2, ignoring alpha. File content/dimensions are not rebound to recorded digests. Keep those limitations visible; no observed product tampering or nonopaque capture was demonstrated.'),
 ('Product and lane publish completion at different stages','Product::complete sees pre-export outcome; diagnostics attachment and shared receipt writing can still fail afterward.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lane.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lib.rs','ports/graphshell/src/web_tree/lane.rs'], 'Graphshell publishes its browser result from complete. It does not override diagnostic_attachment, and browser lanes ordinarily lack a filesystem receipt. Therefore source proves an ordering seam for other consumers, not a newly demonstrated false Graphshell result.'),
 ('CPU timing receipts explicitly limit their success claim','Costs excludes capture/invalid samples and labels host CPU wall time, not GPU duration.', ['crates/cambium/mesquite/src/cost.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/cost/tests.rs'], 'Stage times overlap, capture completion is separate, sample/phase budgets refuse excess, and Lane records observe errors. Costs::finish alone does not rereport a previous budget failure, but the normal Lane preserves the original failure. Do not invent a positive lane receipt by ignoring that error path.'),
 ('Custom leaf state and rendered cache need shared incarnation custody','LeafRegistry and RenderedLeaves are independently keyed by u64.', ['crates/cambium/sprigging/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/sprigging/src/slot.rs'], 'Q324 proves replacement can retain the retired scene or skip the replacement entirely. Path-B scenes are CPU descriptions until the host rasterizes; a registry pass is not GPU acceptance. Path-A/Path-B helpers share one paint vocabulary but the chosen kind is sticky through prior-scene carry.'),
 ('Dirty flags do not cover every public paint input','Stock leaves combine private dirty flags with mutable public styling.', ['crates/cambium/sprigging/src/glyphs.rs','crates/cambium/sprigging/src/angle.rs','crates/cambium/sprigging/src/dimension.rs','crates/cambium/sprigging/src/lib.rs'], 'Q325 proves paint/current hit disagreement through live public APIs. New-leaf constructor styling is safe because it starts dirty. Other setters normalize and dirty their own data; that does not validate unrestricted public styling.'),
 ('GraphGlyph really is the same renderer as GraphCanvas','The compatibility name is a Rust type alias; view hit projection calls GraphViewport::project.', ['crates/cambium/sprigging/src/glyphs.rs','crates/cambium/cambium/src/graph_canvas.rs'], 'Endpoint edges and authored multi-point routes paint through one GraphCanvas. Atlas polygons/compound paths are caller-projected leaf-local paint, while normalized nodes/routes pass through the viewport. Retain the actual distinction rather than labeling the alias another silo.'),
 ('Leaf event/action types remain inert placeholders','LeafEvent and LeafAction carry no payload and Leaf::event defaults to None.', ['crates/cambium/sprigging/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/sprigging/src/glyphs.rs'], 'Knob accessibility declares slider actions; actual host/caller routing must supply behavior. Meter says it never lands in the routable set, but Q315 already shows the native adapter inserts all DOM nodes before publication filtering. GraphCanvas accessibility now preserves an existing label, which does not resolve Q316 for arbitrary hooks.'),
 ('Arrangement/grid geometry is shared but scroll policy remains caller-owned','GridSpec delegates virtualization to VirtualWindow and Cambium builds real DOM rows.', ['crates/cambium/sprigging/src/arrange.rs','crates/cambium/sprigging/src/grid.rs','crates/cambium/cambium/src/grid.rs'], 'VirtualWindow clamps its end but can return start>end for scroll beyond the collection and has unchecked arithmetic for extreme inputs. Cambium explicitly tells callers to clamp via max_scroll; do not call every out-of-contract overscroll a proven product outage.'),
 ('Standalone smoke assembles a second host path','The browser smoke manually builds DOM/layout/translation/device/surface/presentation instead of using the maintained web host.', ['crates/cambium/examples/genet_web_smoke/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/examples/genet_web_smoke/Cargo.toml','crates/cambium/examples/genet_web_smoke/.cargo/config.toml'], 'It is an isolated one-frame engine smoke, not a full browser application. Comments retain old genet-root commands and same-revision pin wording while manifests use branch main. Q327 qualifies the title sentinel. Native builds cfg out essentially all execution; no wasm compile/browser execution was run here.'),
 ('Nested CI is leftover source rather than the repository workflow owner','crates/cambium/.github/workflows/ci.yml is nested beneath the repository root.', ['crates/cambium/.github/workflows/ci.yml','crates/cambium/.gitattributes'], 'The root workflow directory instead contains portable.yml and rust-policy.yml. A nested former-project workflow does not itself run as this repository GitHub Actions CI; source lists old cambium-nematic packaging commands. Do not use its cargo test line as evidence this current full graph is gated.'),
 ('Disabled menu selection is guarded at actual product execution','Graphshell run re-reads the current catalogue and returns when disabled_reason is present.', ['ports/graphshell/src/web_tree/commands.rs','crates/cambium/command-menu/src/session.rs'], 'This closes the prior source follow-up for this consumer: chosen may return disabled, but run refuses it. The shared API source test is intentional; no disabled command execution bug is claimed from that test.')
]
